// src/v4/lens/affected_set.dag
//
// Scope: affected-set lens — given a diff over the dependency graph, derive the MINIMAL subgraph that must re-execute. Canonical authority for incremental execution + CI job selection. scripts/detect-affected-components.sh is the interim BOOTSTRAP BRIDGE; this lens is the structural authority that replaces it (per feedback_no_textual_enforcement_bridges).
// Anchor: THESIS "Free consequences" §205-210 (incremental cross-run execution) + v4-close-interrogation.md §2.5.F affected-set + memory: feedback_no_textual_enforcement_bridges
// Why EARLY (operator 2026-05-15: "something i wanted to get working
//   very early on"): load-bearing for incremental execution AND it is
//   the structural replacement for the shell script currently gating
//   v2/v3/v4 CI selection. Phase 1.5.
//
// Owns:
//   - affected_set: (Dag, Diff) -> Witness<ReExecFrontier>
//     (the minimal node set that must re-run; everything else is
//     incrementally skippable because pure + unchanged)
//     (`Diff` is the std/node.dag D1 type — Path/Edit/Diff;
//      this lens CONSUMES it, it does not own it. The frontier seed is
//      the set of changed Paths; "unchanged" is `content_hash` (B1)
//      equality — the structural-caching dual already stated below.
//      The D1 OPERATION `apply_diff` lives in lens/application.dag,
//      not here: affected_set only reads the Diff, never applies it.)
//   - composes with compiler/05_eval.dag (skip unchanged pure subgraphs)
//   - composes with workflow/ci.dag (gate/job selection — replaces the
//     interim scripts/detect-affected-components.sh shell bridge)
//   - structural caching is the DUAL of the affected set — the SAME
//     mechanism, not a separate system. A build/exec artifact's cache key
//     IS `content_hash` (B1, std/node.dag) of its input subgraph: the
//     affected set names what changed (re-run); a cache restores what did
//     NOT (skip the work). Purity + content-addressing make every
//     artifact memoizable by construction (THESIS "free consequences:
//     automatic memoization") — caching is this lens read the other way.
//     ONE content-hash keys a CI artifact cache, a remote build cache, or
//     a local memo table equally; the backend (e.g. GHA `actions/cache`)
//     is just an emission target of the hash.
//
// WORKED EXAMPLES — the T-21 design contract (SUBSUMED from #3153
// "v4 affected-set: worked-example design contract", which had no
// worker; superseded by this branch per operator 2026-05-15). NODE is
// the ONE real granularity (operator-corrected): "file/module-affected"
// is node granularity PROJECTED UP (files containing ≥1 affected node),
// never a second tier. Diff is STRUCTURAL: a node is "changed" iff its
// B1 content_hash differs from the prior pin — never a textual git diff.
//
//   Graph (→ = "depends on"; content_hash per node, B1):
//     n_reason (a NamedReason variant set in std/diagnostic.dag)
//        ← n_diag (Diagnostic{reason}) ← n_emitR (a Rust emit rule)
//        ← n_diag                       ← n_evalD (eval's diag path)
//     n_pure (a pure helper, independent of n_reason)
//     n_log  (effectful Transform; signature carries the effect per B3,
//             e.g. `-> Eff<Stderr> Unit`) ← n_evalD
//
//   Ex.1 add a NamedReason variant → content_hash(n_reason) changed →
//     forward-closure frontier { n_reason, n_diag, n_emitR, n_evalD };
//     n_pure SKIPPED (inputs unchanged ∧ pure ⇒ provably same output,
//     THESIS:205-210).
//   Ex.2 reformat a comment / rename a local → content_hash UNCHANGED
//     (canonical-form + opaque Symbol, K-1/B1 α-equivalence) → Diff ∅ →
//     frontier ∅, zero recompute. The payoff, BY the hash.
//   Ex.3 change a node whose effect cannot be bounded → FAIL-CLOSED:
//     include dependents, never optimistic skip (no-engine).
//   Ex.4 change n_pure only → frontier { n_pure }; the rest SKIP.
//     Minimal by construction (forward-closure = the affected cone).
//
//   ADVERSARIAL minimality stress (no-engine applied to the FEATURE —
//   construct the edit that breaks minimality if the model is wrong):
//   Ex.R1 effectful local edit: edit n_log's BODY only (reword its
//     Stderr message); signature/effect UNCHANGED. Minimal frontier =
//     { n_log, n_evalD } (the Stderr-cone ONLY) IFF effects are
//     fine-grained — the effect-GRANULARITY contract, NOW ENCODED as
//     lens/effect.dag B-5 (was "implied" in #3153): coarse effects ⇒
//     cone = all effectful nodes ⇒ correct-but-useless.
//   Ex.R1' CONSUMER-RELATIVE (DI) — worth recording for later readers.
//     "Affected" is relative to WHICH graph. With effects-as-parameters
//     (DI-by-construction, the lens/effect.dag B-5 COROLLARY) a unit
//     test injecting a MOCK carrier has its B-4 edge to the mock `Node`,
//     not the real effectful fn — so editing that fn's body SKIPS the
//     mock-injected unit test automatically and RE-RUNS only the
//     integration test that passed the real carrier. No unit-vs-
//     integration mode in this lens; it falls out of each test's
//     DI-resolved graph. Honest boundary: a re-run integration test
//     whose behavior changed may have a STALE expected value — this
//     lens surfaces "re-run", it NEVER rewrites the expectation
//     (no-engine; updating the TestClaim is a deliberate human act).
//     That failure is the intended signal, not a defect.
//   Ex.R2 widely-shared sub-node, partial change (the DOMINANT gate):
//     n_reason consumed by 50+ sites; edit ONE variant only n_emitR
//     matches → minimal frontier = { changed variant sub-Node, n_emitR,
//     its dependents }; the sites on unchanged variants SKIP — IFF
//     dependency edges are NODE-PRECISE (to the consumed sub-Node, not
//     the declaration). NOW ENCODED as compiler/04_infer.dag B-4 (was
//     "implied" in #3153) — the dominant minimality gate, > effects.
//   Ex.R3 "what counts as changed" is safe BY CONSTRUCTION. Per B-3
//     (the #3157 B1-CANON point-3 correction, drafted): child order is
//     UNCONDITIONALLY list-order — the commutative-quotient is
//     structurally foreclosed (no order on opaque Hash; algebra
//     unreachable from the consumes-nothing root). So no
//     "not-proven-commutative reorder" category exists: "changed" =
//     list-order content_hash difference, full stop. The only unsafe
//     direction (a hash collision = missed change) is foreclosed by the
//     hash; cosmetic-reorder over-fire cannot even arise. (If #3157
//     keeps the algebra-derived framing instead, the worst case
//     degrades only to SAFE over-fire — no residual research risk.)
//
// DOGFOOD REALITY (v2 frozen seed; honest, verified 2026-05-15): v2 has
// a `run` interpreter + emits a MODULE-level `dag-artifact.json`, NOT
// the Node tree — and v2 is frozen (A3, cannot enrich its emission). So
// there is NO node-granularity path through v2; node-granularity
// arrives with the v4 pipeline at T-9. Earliest HONEST dogfood =
// MODULE-granularity over `dag-artifact.json` via `v2-compiler run`,
// once v4 files carry real import/declarations AND the v2-interpreter
// pre-flight verifies `v2-compiler run` can execute this lens over the
// artifact. A demo over edge-empty stubs would be theater (forbidden,
// no-engine) — not built.
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag (incl. the D1 Diff type), std/witness.dag
//   - lens/effect.dag (B-5): per-Arrow-Node effect granularity is the
//     R1 usefulness contract (Ex.R1) — coarse effects ⇒ useless cone
//   - compiler/04_infer.dag: the typed dependency graph (Dag). The
//     use→def edges are NOT a stored field (IR-1 freezes InferredFacts
//     at 4) and NOT carried by `resolved_type` (that is the node's
//     type — lossy for binding). Per B-4 the named carrier is the
//     post-resolution opaque `Symbol` (K-1) on each name-ref `Atom`,
//     AUTHORED by compiler/03_resolve.dag (binding = `Symbol`
//     equality) and preserved unchanged through 04_infer. This lens
//     DERIVES the graph by `Symbol`-equality TRAVERSAL over the
//     resolved tree (node.dag `name_occurrences` pattern); it stores
//     no dependency-edge set. Frontier minimality depends on that
//     binding being NODE-PRECISE (exact declaration, not
//     module/scope); coarse binding = correct but maximally
//     over-firing.
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-21
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).

module v4.lens.affected_set

